# REED PROJECT INTEL SKILL

## PURPOSE
REED intel is the ammunition that makes DBW reps
sound like insiders instead of telemarketers. When
a rep says I was talking to the Director of Public
Works over at the city — he mentioned you guys won
the project name — the contractor assumes it is a
warm relationship. Your job is to find that intel
fast, accurately, and in enough depth to load the
rep with multiple name-drops and conversation angles.

## INPUTS REQUIRED
Company name and city and state.

## STEP 1 — TANGO PRIMARY SOURCE
Tango searches US government contracting data
including awarded contracts, active bids, and
DOT projects.

Search approach: use search_opportunities with
company name plus state to get the project list.
Then use get_details on each result to pull full
project info including all bidders.
Also search city plus construction type if the
company name returns nothing — try city plus paving
or city plus utilities or city plus highway.

Pull 2 to 3 projects per company, most recent first.

From get_details extract: project name and scope
description, award date or bid date, awarding
authority including city or county or DOT district
or school board, contract value, the complete
bidder list showing every company that submitted
a bid not just the winner, and project status.

The bidder list is gold. These are companies doing
the same work in the same market. The rep can call
all of them. List every single one.

## STEP 2 — ZOOMINFO SCOOPS
After Tango, run enrich_scoops and enrich_news on
the company. Scoops may reveal project wins,
equipment purchases, expansions, and new contracts.
News may mention specific awarded contracts not in
Tango's database. A scoop saying just won a large
highway contract in a city is usable project intel
even without a full bid record.

## STEP 3 — TAVILY BACKUP
Use only if Tango and scoops return nothing.
Run one search using this query format:
company name plus city plus state plus construction
contract awarded bid won 2024 2025 2026 public
works DOT project bidders.

Extract all three from this one call: project names
and scope, Director of Public Works name, and other
bidders. Also try searching city plus state plus
ConstructConnect awarded contracts 2025 2026 to
find city-level project activity.

## CONFIDENCE RULE
Government database results from Tango: include them.
Government website results via Tavily: include them.
News article confirming an award: include it.
ZoomInfo scoop: include it and note the source.
Cannot verify: write No verified project found.
Never fabricate project names, PWD names, or bidder
company names under any circumstances.

## WHEN NO PROJECT IS FOUND
Write: No verified project found — use general
DOT name-drop. Then provide the Director of Public
Works name from Tango or Tavily search if found,
and provide this general opener for the rep to use:
I work with the city Department of Public Works and
several contractors doing paving or utilities or
commercial work in the area.

## OUTPUT FORMAT
Return the following block for each company:

PROJECT 1 most recent:
Name and description of project name and scope.
Awarded: month and year.
Awarding Authority: city or county or state DOT
or school district.
Project location: city and county.
Contract Value: dollar amount if found.
Status: In Bid or Awarded or Active or Completed.
All Bidders Found: list every company that bid,
typically 5 to 15 companies.

PROJECT 2 previous: same format.
PROJECT 3 older: same format if found.

Director of Public Works: name, title, city or county.
Other Key Name Drops: any project stakeholders,
city engineers, or DOT contacts found.

## OPENING LINE CONSTRUCTION
Once REED intel is in hand, pass the PWD name and
the top 1 to 2 competing bidder names to the
dbw-opening-lines skill as name drop inputs.
Those become the backbone of the cold call opener
that makes the rep sound like an insider.